Konstantin Dmitriev · 117th in this Competition · Posted 2 months ago
Google Perch model is quite good as a baseline
Google's Perch model for bird identification (https://www.kaggle.com/models/google/bird-vocalization-classifier) was updated this year. It shows a significant improvement on 2025 data, and it can predict 203 out of 234 species in the current competition (all Aves and most of Amphibia).

I tried Perch model in this notebook, and it yielded me a good score of 0.825.

The prediction takes almost 90 minutes and finishes just in time. There were some issues with the TF version, as Perch seems to require the latest.


